{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.BarApplyTransfer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.BarApplyTransfer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.bar_apply_transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.bar_apply_transfer","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-apply-transfer.lean#L77-L85","doc":"**Bar-transfer principle** (Proposition):\n\nCombines the lower-bound transfer and the negation transfer\ninto the headline statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bar-apply-transfer","label":"prop:bar-apply-transfer","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-apply-transfer.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.neg_transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.neg_transfer","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-apply-transfer.lean#L66-L75","doc":"**Negation transfer**: a counterexample to P at q < a (with q > 0)\ntransports along bar to a counterexample at q⁻¹ > a⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.bar_apply_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.bar_apply_lower","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-apply-transfer.lean#L51-L64","doc":"A simpler form of the transfer lemma that avoids the iff:\nif P holds on (a, ∞) and P is bar-invariant, then P holds on\n(0, a⁻¹) (positive part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.lower_bound_transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.lower_bound_transfer","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-apply-transfer.lean#L28-L49","doc":"**Lower-bound transfer**: for a bar-invariant property,\n\"P holds for all q > a\" is equivalent to\n\"P holds for all q ∈ (0, a⁻¹)\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.BarInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarApplyTransfer.BarInvariant","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-apply-transfer.lean#L24-L26","doc":"A property is **bar-invariant** if P(q) ↔ P(q⁻¹) for every q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0}]}